Wayland: fullscreen on the monitor the window is currently on.

GLFW's API requires naming a monitor for fullscreen, but on Wayland a
client cannot know which output a window is on (window positions are
hidden from clients), so any explicit choice is a guess — typically the
output at the layout origin. The Wayland protocol handles this natively:
xdg_toplevel_set_fullscreen(NULL) lets the compositor pick the output the
window is currently on (this is what mpv does). Pass NULL instead of the
requested monitor's output for runtime fullscreen toggles
(glfwSetWindowMonitor -> acquireMonitor); the monitor argument still
selects the video mode reported to the app.

--- a/src/wl_window.c
+++ b/src/wl_window.c
@@ -503,12 +503,12 @@
     if (window->wl.libdecor.frame)
     {
         libdecor_frame_set_fullscreen(window->wl.libdecor.frame,
-                                      window->monitor->wl.output);
+                                      NULL);
     }
     else if (window->wl.xdg.toplevel)
     {
         xdg_toplevel_set_fullscreen(window->wl.xdg.toplevel,
-                                    window->monitor->wl.output);
+                                    NULL);
     }
 
     setIdleInhibitor(window, GLFW_TRUE);
